  "question": {
    "text": "<strong>Paragraph:</strong>\nLet $V_r$ denotes the sum of the first $r$ terms of an arithmetic progression $(A P)$ whose first term is $r$ and the common difference is $(2 r-1)$. Let $T_r=V_{r+1}-V_r-2$ and $Q_r=T_{r+1}-T_r$ for $r=1,2, \\ldots$<strong>Question:</strong>\n$T_r$ is always",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "gvHPO",
      "text": "\nan odd number\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2Hn9A",
      "text": "\nan even number\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "yNwup",
      "text": "\na prime number\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "WM1as",
      "text": "\na composite number",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$V_{r+1}-V_r=(r+1)^3-r^3-\\frac{1}{2}\\left[(r+1)^2-r^2\\right]+\\frac{1}{2}(1)$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& =3 r^2+2 r+1 \\\\\n\\therefore \\quad T_r & =3 r^2+2 r-1=(r+1)(3 r-1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nwhich is a composite number.",
    "image": null
  },
